.TH LEMUX 1 2026-11-21 "lemux 0.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lemux \- check, clean, remove, install and update a Linux system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lemux
.RB [ \-y ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lemux
is a small assistant for everyday Linux maintenance. It reports the health of the
system and repairs what it can, frees space taken by caches that rebuild themselves,
removes applications and matching user files, and installs and
updates AppImages as if they were regular applications.
.PP
It drives the tools your distribution already ships (apt, dnf, pacman, zypper,
systemd, Flatpak, Snap) instead of replacing them. Cleanup and native removal commands preview changes until given
.BR \-\-apply .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-watch "] [" \-n
.IR seconds ]
One-screen dashboard: health score (0\(en100), CPU, memory, swap, disk usage and
I/O, network traffic, temperature, battery, failed units and top processes.
.B \-\-watch
refreshes it until Ctrl+C.
.TP
.BR analyze " [\fIfolder\fR] [" \-\-top
.IR N ]
Largest folders directly under a folder (default: home), with their share of the
total, and the largest files below it. Read-only; stays on one filesystem.
.TP
.BR history " [" \-n
.IR N "] [" \fB\-\-json\fR ]
What
.B lemux
deleted, moved to the Trash, uninstalled or optimized.
.TP
.BR purge " [\fIfolder\fR ...] [" \-\-apply "] [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-days
.IR N ]
Deletes rebuildable build artifacts of your projects (node_modules, .svelte\-kit,
\&.next, target, Composer vendor, Python venvs and caches, Gradle, build/dist, Dart,
Swift and Zig caches). Each must sit next to the file that proves what it is, nothing
tracked by git is touched, and artifacts changed in the last
.I N
days (default 7) are kept unless
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.BR installers " [" \-\-apply "] [" \-\-all ]
Installer files in Downloads, Telegram Desktop and the Desktop. Packages that are
already installed and AppImages identical to one managed by
.B lemux
are selected for the Trash; other installers need
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.BR optimize " [" \-\-apply ]
Flushes the DNS cache, rebuilds the application menu, MIME, icon and font caches,
runs TRIM when no fstrim timer is active. Only the steps that apply to the system are shown.
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-fix ]
Health report for clock, audio, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, services, packages, memory,
swap, storage, temperatures and the systemd journal.
.B \-\-fix
offers, one by one, the repairs
.B lemux
knows for the problems found. Exits 1 when there are warnings.
.TP
.BR clean " [" \-\-apply "] [" \-\-trash "] [" \-\-orphans "] [" \-\-journal "] [" \-\-packages ]
Reports the space held by browser caches (skipped while the browser runs), npm,
pnpm, Yarn, pip, Go, Composer, Corepack, Cargo downloads and thumbnails.
.B \-\-packages
also cleans the native package cache.
.B \-\-apply
deletes them;
.B \-\-trash
also empties the Trash;
.B \-\-orphans
removes packages nothing depends on;
.B \-\-journal
shrinks the systemd journal to 200M.
.TP
.BI "remove " name " \fR[\fB\-\-apply\fR]"
Finds an exact package or application ID. With
.BR \-\-apply ,
matching user files go to the Trash and file associations are removed.
.TP
.B app install \fIfile.AppImage\fR | \fIowner/repo\fR | \fIGitHub URL\fR \fR[\fB\-\-from \fIowner/repo\fR] [\fB\-\-name \fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-move\fR]
Installs an AppImage under
.IR ~/.local/share/lemux/apps/<id> ,
with a generated menu entry from AppImage metadata, an icon when available, and a
command in
.IR ~/.local/bin .
The update source is the GitHub repository given with
.BR \-\-from ,
or the repository used for the initial installation.
.B \-\-move
sends the original local file to the Trash after installation.
.TP
.B app update \fR[\fIid\fR ...] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Updates AppImages. GitHub downloads require a matching SHA-256 digest.
A previous version is kept for rollback. Set a source with
.BR "\-\-from owner/repo" .
.B app update \fIid file.AppImage
updates from a local file.
.TP
.B app list\fR, \fBapp rollback \fIid\fR, \fBapp remove \fIid \fR[\fB\-\-purge\fR]
List installed AppImages, return to the previous version, or uninstall
.RB ( \-\-purge
also moves matching user files to the Trash).
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-apps ]
Upgrades system packages (after asking), Flatpak and Snap apps, and the
AppImages installed with
.BR lemux .
.B \-\-apps
updates only the AppImages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Answer yes to every confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Plain output. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable has the same effect.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help; every command also accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH SAFETY
Use
.B \-\-apply
to execute previewed cleanup steps. Root rights are requested for system
operations that need them. When the Trash is unavailable, files selected
for it stay in place.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lemux/protect
Absolute paths or globs, one per line, to keep during file cleanup.
Cleanup is blocked if the protect list cannot be read.
.TP
.I ~/.config/lemux/purge_paths
Folders scanned by
.BR purge .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lemux/operations.log
Every deletion, uninstall and optimization, shown by
.BR history .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/lemux/apps/<id>/
AppImage, icon, metadata and the previous version.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/lemux\-<id>.desktop
Menu entries of managed AppImages.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Raises the GitHub API rate limit for AppImage updates.
.TP
.B LEMUX_YES
Set to 1 to answer yes to confirmations.
.TP
.B LEMUX_NO_OPLOG
Set to 1 to stop writing the operations log.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colours.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure or when
.B check
finds warnings, 2 on wrong usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lemux status \-\-watch
lemux analyze ~/Documents
lemux purge \-\-apply
lemux installers \-\-apply
lemux check \-\-fix
lemux clean                 # see what can be freed
lemux clean \-\-apply \-\-orphans
lemux remove obs\-studio      # review, then add \-\-apply
lemux app install ~/Downloads/Shotcut.AppImage \-\-from mltframework/shotcut
lemux app install neovim/neovim
lemux update
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR zypper (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
